{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b0c2bca985561aa4","name":"Viper Kinrath","source":{"id":"source:reference-b0c2bca985561aa4","title":"Viper Kinrath","revision":21806,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:31:22Z","sha256":"ad4889dfd97d957a0fea5f0d3aceeeef89201dc71423a16f685857761f959761","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21806","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Viper%20Kinrath&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b0c2bca985561aa4","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Creatures of KOTOR"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Creatures_of_KOTOR"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Kinrath and its deadlier variety, the Viper Kinrath shown here, are commonly found on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dantooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dantooine","referenceId":"reference:c24e970214f5ff8b"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"}," but have been spotted on other, more distant planets in smaller numbers. This bizarre insectile creature has four long legs sprouting from a central body. Another long appendage sprouts from the \"face\" of the Viper Kinrath, which ends in a sharp, poison-filled stinger. (Regular ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kinrath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kinrath","referenceId":"reference:64d455d5dcaa0035"}," are functionally the same, but replace their Sting attack with another Slam attack and no Poison.)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Their miniscule eyes are vestigial, and the creature uses a combination of heat sensing and smell to navigate and locate prey. Every Kinrath produces a unique, pungent odor from large sweat glands that allows them to locate each other. Savvy hunters learn to coat themselves with the sweat from these glands in order to move in close to Kinraths and take them unawares.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Jedi and other Force-users have learned that Kinrath eggs contain red crystals that can be used as the power source for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},". Indeed, many Padawans are sent to hunt for these eggs as part of their final test to create their own ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Viper Kinrath Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Kinrath are found throughout ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dantooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dantooine","referenceId":"reference:c24e970214f5ff8b"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"},", although they typically stick close to large clumps of vegetation where their natural coloration helps them blend into their surroundings. Unlucky heroes may stumble into a Kinrath hive and confront the hive queen, protected by dozens of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kinrath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kinrath","referenceId":"reference:64d455d5dcaa0035"}," and Viper Kinrath. As mentioned above, young Jedi might have to hunt Kinrath to gather eggs and the crystals inside to manufacture their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Viper Kinrath Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":